</p>
 
<h2 class="mt-14">Consent and purchaser suppression for Ab testing</h2>
<p>Ab Testing readiness starts with provable consent records and instant post-checkout suppression across each app running ab testing sends. For ab testing, a promo arriving after a purchase, refund, or open support case burns trust faster than weak ab testing creative ever could.</p>
<div class="overflow-x-auto mb-8"><table>
<thead><tr><th>Audience state</th><th>Required handling</th><th>Why it matters</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>No documented consent</td><td>Ab Testing marketing stays off; transactional only</td><td>Consent evidence underwrites all ab testing sending</td></tr>
<tr><td>Consented, never purchased</td><td>Open ab testing with guidance and proof, not discounts</td><td>Early ab testing discounts train deal-waiting</td></tr>
<tr><td>Active cart, no checkout</td><td>Remind ab testing carts with context first, no instant code</td><td>Margin-safe ab testing recovery at peak intent</td></tr>
<tr><td>Purchased recently</td><td>Ab Testing buyers get education, not another pitch</td><td>Keeps ab testing buyers from instant list fatigue</td></tr>
<tr><td>Refund or return open</td><td>Hold ab testing marketing while service cases stay open</td><td>Open ab testing cases reset what the shopper tolerates</td></tr>
<tr><td>Repeated non-engagement</td><td>Remove chronic ab testing non-openers pre-complaint</td><td>Keeps ab testing placement high via list hygiene</td></tr>
<tr><td>SMS consent present</td><td>Ab Testing texting respects time and frequency rules</td><td>One ab testing SMS complaint outweighs many email ones</td></tr>
<tr><td>Wholesale or B2B account</td><td>Send ab testing B2B accounts down their own track</td><td>B2B ab testing mis-sends risk contract breach</td></tr>
<tr><td>Free or disposable email domain</td><td>Verify ab testing throwaway addresses pre-journey</td><td>Low-grade ab testing signups drag deliverability</td></tr>
<tr><td>Staff and test accounts</td><td>Ab Testing QA profiles excluded from reporting</td><td>Internal ab testing activity corrupts program metrics</td></tr>
<tr><td>Competitor or researcher signals</td><td>Treat ab testing snoops under normal consent policy</td><td>Ab Testing consistency beats clever carve-outs</td></tr>
<tr><td>Legacy list without timestamps</td><td>Ab Testing sends to old lists need fresh opt-in</td><td>Timestamp-less ab testing consent is legal exposure</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<h2 class="mt-12">Margin, app costs, and pricing for Ab testing</h2>
<p>For ab testing, revenue attribution flatters; margin decides. Burden the ab testing program with its true load — platform fees, overages, SMS, capture, creative, agency, and ab testing discount cost — before calling it profitable. When the ab testing stack nears fifteen percent of email-attributed margin, simplify the ab testing setup before tuning it.</p>
<p>Pricing changes frequently and varies by region, contact volume, and contract term, so check the official pricing pages of every shortlisted app and model an eighteen-month total that includes a peak season. For ab testing, free plans always bind somewhere; identify whether contacts, sends, branching, or support caps your ab testing motion first.</p>
<div class="overflow-x-auto mb-8"><table>
<thead><tr><th>Cost component</th><th>What to model</th><th>Common failure</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Platform subscription</td><td>Ab Testing tier matched to true contact volume</td><td>ab testing plan sized for hopes, not contacts</td></tr>
<tr><td>Contact or send overages</td><td>Ab Testing headroom checked against growth</td><td>Peak ab testing volume blowing past tier limits</td></tr>
<tr><td>SMS credits</td><td>ab testing SMS units from opt-in rate and flow depth</td><td>Treating ab testing texts like near-free email</td></tr>
<tr><td>Discount budget</td><td>ab testing promo cost from depth-times-redemption</td><td>ab testing incentives training perpetual waiting</td></tr>
<tr><td>Creative and ops time</td><td>Weekly ab testing hours to run and QA flows</td><td>ab testing upkeep heavier than budgeted</td></tr>
<tr><td>Migration and setup</td><td>Ab Testing import, consent mapping, flow rebuild</td><td>Ab Testing audit trail gaps after moves</td></tr>
<tr><td>Support and success tiers</td><td>Does ab testing crisis support cost extra</td><td>Ab Testing help-desk limits exposed by drops</td></tr>
<tr><td>Third-party integrations</td><td>Ab Testing review, loyalty, capture add-ons</td><td>ab testing side-tools eclipsing core cost</td></tr>
<tr><td>Deliverability remediation</td><td>Ab Testing reputation maintenance budget</td><td>Ab Testing inbox harm priced above the plan</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
